  "intro": "L'Hopital's Rule evaluates limits in the indeterminate forms $\\frac{0}{0}$ or $\\frac{\\infty}{\\infty}$: if $\\lim\\frac{f}{g}$ has that form and $f,g$ are differentiable, then $\\lim\\dfrac{f(x)}{g(x)}=\\lim\\dfrac{f'(x)}{g'(x)}$, provided the right side exists. Always confirm the indeterminate form first, differentiate numerator and denominator separately (not as a quotient), and repeat if the new limit is still indeterminate.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{\\sin x}{x}$ using L'Hopital's Rule.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Substitution gives $\\frac{0}{0}$, so the rule applies.",
          "Differentiate top and bottom: $\\frac{\\cos x}{1}$.",
          "Evaluate at $x=0$: $\\frac{\\cos 0}{1}=\\frac{1}{1}=1$."
        ],
        "answer": "$1$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{e^x-1}{x}$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Form is $\\frac{0}{0}$.",
          "Differentiate: $\\frac{e^x}{1}$.",
          "At $x=0$: $\\frac{1}{1}=1$."
        ],
        "answer": "$1$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\dfrac{\\ln x}{x}$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "As $x\\to\\infty$ the form is $\\frac{\\infty}{\\infty}$.",
          "Differentiate: $\\frac{1/x}{1}=\\frac{1}{x}$.",
          "As $x\\to\\infty$, $\\frac{1}{x}\\to 0$."
        ],
        "answer": "$0$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{1-\\cos x}{x^2}$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$\\frac{0}{0}$; differentiate: $\\frac{\\sin x}{2x}$, still $\\frac{0}{0}$.",
          "Apply again: $\\frac{\\cos x}{2}\\to\\frac{1}{2}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 5,
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\dfrac{x^2}{e^x}$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$\\frac{\\infty}{\\infty}$; differentiate twice: $\\frac{2x}{e^x}\\to\\frac{2}{e^x}\\to 0$."
        ],
        "answer": "$0$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 6,
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\lim_{x\\to 1}\\dfrac{\\ln x}{x-1}$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "$\\frac{0}{0}$; differentiate: $\\frac{1/x}{1}=\\frac{1}{x}\\to 1$."
        ],
        "answer": "$1$"
      }
    }
